WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.083 --> 00:00:01.876
- [Narrator] Here's how I
prepare for my coding interview.

00:00:01.876 --> 00:00:04.671
I solve 1,513 leetcode problems.

00:00:04.671 --> 00:00:06.131
Memorize all of the answers,

00:00:06.131 --> 00:00:08.299
read "Cracking the Coding
Interview" five times,

00:00:08.299 --> 00:00:09.926
read "Elements of Programming Interviews"

00:00:09.926 --> 00:00:11.302
in all three languages.

00:00:11.302 --> 00:00:13.430
Python, C++ and Spanish.

00:00:15.306 --> 00:00:17.350
Read "Grokking the
Systems Design Interview."

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:18.309
Don't understand shit,

00:00:18.309 --> 00:00:19.686
but memorize every keyword.

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:21.938
Sharding, caching, load balancing.

00:00:21.938 --> 00:00:23.189
Damn, I'm so smart.

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:25.066
Go on LinkedIn to stalk my interviewer.

00:00:25.066 --> 00:00:25.900
Check their Facebook,

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:26.735
check their Twitter,

00:00:26.735 --> 00:00:27.569
check their Wife.

00:00:29.237 --> 00:00:31.281
Hm. Nice.

00:00:31.281 --> 00:00:32.407
Go on on Glassdoor to find

00:00:32.407 --> 00:00:34.576
the interview questions they ask.

00:00:34.576 --> 00:00:35.577
Not good enough.

00:00:35.577 --> 00:00:36.870
Pay lots of money to access

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:37.996
a sketchy Chinese website

00:00:37.996 --> 00:00:39.664
to get leaked interview questions.

00:00:39.664 --> 00:00:40.498
Perfect.

00:00:40.498 --> 00:00:41.332
I go to the bathroom

00:00:41.332 --> 00:00:42.625
for my breathing exercise.

00:00:47.714 --> 00:00:49.257
Fucking love meditating.

00:00:49.257 --> 00:00:51.134
The company is calling
me for an interview,

00:00:51.134 --> 00:00:52.427
I bring up all my cheat sheets.

00:00:52.427 --> 00:00:53.887
This is child's play.

00:00:53.887 --> 00:00:54.971
I'm ready for this.

00:00:55.847 --> 00:00:57.640
- Hey, thank you so much
for hopping on this call.

00:00:57.640 --> 00:00:58.475
- You're welcome.

00:00:59.976 --> 00:01:01.311
- Yeah, OK.

00:01:01.311 --> 00:01:02.812
So, I'm your interviewer.

00:01:02.812 --> 00:01:05.023
And yeah, so the first question is

00:01:05.023 --> 00:01:06.858
what would you do if you had a conflict

00:01:06.858 --> 00:01:07.692
with your manager?

00:01:07.692 --> 00:01:09.319
- Hashmap, I'll use a Hashmap!

